    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n60407" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῠαθ-ίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ladle out</i> wine, <i><span class="en">
				Antiph.
				115
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Diph.
				107
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ταῖς ναυσὶν ἐκ θαλάττης</span>
			<i>draw water</i> from the sea with the ships (<i>as one draws
				wine</i> from a bowl), of the engines of Archimedes lifting the
			Roman ships out of the water, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				8.6.6
			</span></i>.</div>
